  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 104 AM MDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nToday through Fri night...High pressure slowly breaks down in\nadvance of an incoming trough during this period, starting\nThursday. Until then, expect sunny skies and temperatures\nreturning in lower elevation to above 80 deg F starting today,\nand even warmer Thu. The approaching trough brings cooler air\nand cloud cover, and temperatures will start to cool from Thu to\nFri. There is a very weak chance of precipitation, mainly seen \non ECMWF model runs, for the southern and eastern highlands, \nspilling into the Snake River plain.\n\nWind will be light today, but on Thu afternoon, as the trough\ndraws closer, will increase substantially, with windy conditions\n(20 to 30 mph with gusts to 40 mph) developing. Wind will\ncontinue to be at that level Fri afternoon.\n\nSat through Tue...The trough that brings the wind and a slight\nchance of showers and thunder on Thu night/Fri will cross over\nthe forecast area. This will increase the threat of showers and\nthunderstorms, which will bring significant cooling after the\ntrough passes to the east on Sat night. Temperatures will cool\nby 15 to 20 deg F for afternoon highs. \n\nWind will weaken on Sat, then increase again on Sun in the post\ntrough regime. Mon will see the departure of the trough's\ninfluence, with temperatures starting a warming or at least\nbottoming out, with once again nearly clear skies and a return\nto dry conditions for Mon to the end of the forecast period.\nTemperatures will warm back to near normal by Tue/Wed.",
